  "tag_ids": [],
  "policy_sha256": "84f656b16099dcb248866f714453e5bd3e275bdb5d4929c4fad838ee8b29ed2c",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00001",
      "text": "On January 5, Pakistan's Supreme Court ordered local authorities in the northwest town of Karak to rebuild a Hindu temple and adjacent shrine that were razed by a mob incited by Muslim clerics in the previous week.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 214,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.dawn.com/news/1598812"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00002",
      "text": "The local press says tensions between Karak's Muslim and Hindu communities intensified recently as Hindu leaders obtained permission to extend the temple's site.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 216,
      "body_end": 377,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00003",
      "text": "The perimeter was the subject of a nearly 20-year dispute after a similar attack in 1997 left the temple and the shrine in ruins. Reconstruction didn't begin until 2015, when the Supreme Court demarcated its boundaries and ordered the repairs.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 379,
      "body_end": 622,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.dawn.com/news/1202865"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00004",
      "text": "The police arrested a cleric of the Jamiat Ulema-e-Islam-Fazl (JUI-F), a religious right-wing political party that has a strong presence in the area, and several other perpetrators in connection with the attack. Twelve police officers were also suspended for negligence, local reports say.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 624,
      "body_end": 913,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamiat_Ulema-e-Islam_(F)",
        "https://www.samaa.tv/news/pakistan/2021/01/police-showed-cowardice-in-karak-hindu-temple-attack/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00005",
      "text": "Journalist Mubashir Zaidi tweeted a copy of the complaint police registered against the perpetrators:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 915,
      "body_end": 1016,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00006",
      "text": "And journalist Muhammad Imran tweeted a photo of one of the clerics as he was escorted by the police:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1018,
      "body_end": 1119,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00007",
      "text": "JUI-F representatives condemned the destruction of the temple and claimed that the incident was a “government's conspiracy” to implicate its leaders.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1121,
      "body_end": 1270,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.thenews.com.pk/print/768467-jui-f-sees-conspiracy-behind-hindu-temple-attack"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00008",
      "text": "Hindus make up less than two per cent of Pakistan's 223-million population. Although Pakistan's Constitution guarantees freedom of religion, attacks on Hindu places of worship aren't uncommon.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1272,
      "body_end": 1464,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hinduism_in_Pakistan",
        "https://globalvoices.org/2019/09/19/in-a-pakistani-town-hindu-muslim-relations-are-tested-after-a-hindu-temple-is-vandalised/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00009",
      "text": "In 2020, the United States named Pakistan as a “country of particular concern” for engaging in or tolerating “systematic, ongoing, [and] egregious” religious freedom violations.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 1466,
      "body_end": 1643,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.dawn.com/news/1451399/why-did-us-blacklist-pakistan-for-religious-freedom-violations"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00010",
      "text": "Dr. Zakir Naik, a Muslim preacher and televangelist from India, praised the destruction of the Karak temple on a January 2 video. In July, he also voiced opposition against the construction of a Hindu temple in Pakistan's capital, Islamabad.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 1645,
      "body_end": 1886,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zakir_Naik",
        "https://www.opindia.com/2020/07/zakir-naik-youtube-islamic-pakistan-hindu-temple-haram-islamist-kingdom-destroy-imran-khan/",
        "https://www.timesnownews.com/international/article/zakir-naik-backs-demolition-of-temple-in-pakistan-says-temples-should-not-be-allowed-in-an-islamic-country/701983"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00011",
      "text": "READ MORE: Construction of first Hindu temple in Islamabad faces opposition",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 1888,
      "body_end": 1963,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/2020/07/14/construction-of-first-hindu-temple-in-islamabad-pakistan-faces-opposition/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "h5",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00012",
      "text": "The rebuilding efforts of the Karak temple will take place under the guises of the Evacuee Trust Property Board, a government body that administers property left behind by Hindus and Sikhs who migrated to India after the partition in 1947.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 1965,
      "body_end": 2204,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evacuee_Trust_Property_Board",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partition_of_India",
        "https://www.etpb.gov.pk/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00013",
      "text": "The Supreme Court also ordered the Evacuee Trust Property Board to produce a report on the number of temples (Hindus) and gurdwaras (Sikhs) in Pakistan and the steps taken by the authorities to protect them.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 2206,
      "body_end": 2413,
      "source_links": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evacuee_Trust_Property_Board",
        "https://www.dawn.com/news/1599843/sc-orders-eptb-to-start-reconstruction-of-damaged-hindu-shrine-in-karak"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00014",
      "text": "Reactions",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 14,
      "body_start": 2415,
      "body_end": 2424,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "h3",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00015",
      "text": "Soon after the incident, videos showing the attacks went viral and the hashtag #KarakAttack trended on social media.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 15,
      "body_start": 2426,
      "body_end": 2542,
      "source_links": [
        "https://twitter.com/hashtag/KarakAttack?src=hashtag_click"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00016",
      "text": "Expat Pakistani Aisha Mansoor tweeted:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 16,
      "body_start": 2544,
      "body_end": 2582,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00017",
      "text": "Shaza Fatima Khawaja, a Member National Assembly of Pakistan, tweeted:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 17,
      "body_start": 2584,
      "body_end": 2654,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00018",
      "text": "Educator Javeed Ahmed Khan commented:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 18,
      "body_start": 2656,
      "body_end": 2693,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00019",
      "text": "Twitter user Usman said:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 19,
      "body_start": 2695,
      "body_end": 2719,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00020",
      "text": "In an Op-Ed on Express Tribune, Rustum Shah Mohmand commented:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 20,
      "body_start": 2721,
      "body_end": 2783,
      "source_links": [
        "https://tribune.com.pk/story/2278836/a-vicious-attack"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-725976-b00021",
      "text": "> The pervasive feeling of insecurity amongst ethnic minorities does not augur well for peace and progress. There is a need for course correction and introspection. Providing protection and security to its citizens is a state’s fundamental responsibility. Failure to safeguard minorities is a system failure.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 21,
      "body_start": 2785,
      "body_end": 3093,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    }
  ],
